  "video_id": "wfxKwkKoGtI",
  "title": "5 Free Sites That Made My Claude Builds Look Expensive",
  "description": "AI-built websites look amateur because the model writes animation by hand instead of calling a library that professionals already built. Naming the library in your prompt fixes it faster than any design description.\n\nAnime.js (72,469 stars) for animation. Motion, formerly Framer Motion (33,381 stars), for transitions and state changes. Magic UI (22,083 stars) for animated copy-paste components. shadcn/ui (122,257 stars) for the foundation and for animated dashboard charts. All four are free and MIT licensed. Manus is the fifth, an agent that builds the whole site for you.\n\nGet every link plus the master build prompt here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xJX5V0UXEMwu66qwL_fqStcUP1p40SHbK1NN3at2djc/edit?usp=sharing\n\n#Shorts #WebDesign #ClaudeAI",
